kreuzerSkarke -- access Kreuzer-Skarke dimension 4 reflexive polytopes database
*******************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        kreuzerSkarke(h11, Limit=>n)
        kreuzerSkarke(h11, h12)
        kreuzerSkarke str
  * Inputs:
      * h11, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, The desired Picard number of
        the Calabi-Yau hypersurface, a number between 1 and 491 inclusive.
      * h12, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, (optional) the desired
        $h^{1,2}$ of the Calabi-Yau hypersurface
      * str, a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String,, parses the given string
        into a list of KSEntry's
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Limit (missing documentation) => an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,,
        default value 1000, The maximum number of examples to retrieve
      * Vertices (missing documentation) => an *note integer:
        (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, default value null, Restrict to those examples with
        this number of vertices
      * Facets (missing documentation) => an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,,
        default value null, Restrict to those examples with this number of
        facets
      * LatticePoints (missing documentation) => an *note integer:
        (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, default value null, Restrict to those examples with
        this number of lattice points
      * DualLatticePoints (missing documentation) => an *note integer:
        (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, default value null, Restrict to those examples whose
        polar dual has this number of lattice points
      * H12 (missing documentation) => an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,,
        default value null, Restrict to those examples whose associated
        Calabi-Yau 3-fold has the given $h^{1,2}(X)$
      * Access (missing documentation) => a *note string:
        (Macaulay2Doc)String,, default value null, Either null (use Macaulay2's
        getWWW), "wget" or "curl".  Mainly an internal optional argument for
        developers
  * Outputs:
      * a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, of *note KSEntry: KSEntry,'s, each
        of which is one entry (one polytope) from the database. Use *note
        matrix(KSEntry): matrix_lpKSEntry_rp, and *note description(KSEntry):
        description, to extract information from an entry.

Description
===========

As a an example, let's take the 4th example with $h^{11}=5$, $h^{21}=53$.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : topes = kreuzerSkarke(5, 53, Limit=>4)                                  |
|using offline data file: ks5+53-n204.txt                                     |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = {4 5  M:51 5 N:11 5 H:5,53 [-96] id:0, 4 5  M:61 5 N:9 5 H:5,53 [-96]   |
|         1   0   1   1  -8                     1   0   0   4  -8             |
|         0   1   0   0  -3                     0   1   1   9 -15             |
|         0   0   3   3 -12                     0   0   2   0  -6             |
|         0   0   0   6 -12                     0   0   0  12 -12             |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     id:1, 4 9  M:60 9 N:10 6 H:5,53 [-96] id:2, 4 9  M:59 9 N:10 6 H:5,53   |
|              1   1   1   1   0  -1  -1  -2  -4     1   1   1   0   0   0    |
|              0   3   0   1   0  -1  -4   0  -4     0   2   0   0   4   0    |
|              0   0   2   2   0   2   2  -6  -4     0   0   2   0   0   4    |
|              0   0   0   0   1  -2  -2   3   1     0   0   0   1   1   1    |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     [-96] id:3}                                                             |
|     -2  -2  -2                                                              |
|     -4  -6  -6                                                              |
|     -6  -6  -4                                                              |
|     -3  -3  -3                                                              |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : assert(#topes == 4)                                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : tope = topes_3                                                          |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = 4 9  M:59 9 N:10 6 H:5,53 [-96] id:3                                    |
|        1   1   1   0   0   0  -2  -2  -2                                    |
|        0   2   0   0   4   0  -4  -6  -6                                    |
|        0   0   2   0   0   4  -6  -6  -4                                    |
|        0   0   0   1   1   1  -3  -3  -3                                    |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : KSEntry                                                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : header = description tope                                               |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = 4 9  M:59 9 N:10 6 H:5,53 [-96] id:3                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : A = matrix tope                                                         |
|                                                                             |
|o5 = | 1 1 1 0 0 0 -2 -2 -2 |                                                |
|     | 0 2 0 0 4 0 -4 -6 -6 |                                                |
|     | 0 0 2 0 0 4 -6 -6 -4 |                                                |
|     | 0 0 0 1 1 1 -3 -3 -3 |                                                |
|                                                                             |
|              4       9                                                      |
|o5 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

The description line gives some information about the example, see *note
Kreuzer-Skarke description headers: Kreuzer-Skarke description headers, for
more details. The polytope is the convex hull of the columns of the matrix $A$.

Some of the Kreuzer-Skarke data is available from this package off-line.  To
see what is available when not connected to the net, or when the website is
down, call *note availableOffline: availableOffline,.

