kreuzerSkarkeDim3 -- the list of 4319 dimension 3 reflexive polytopes in the Kreuzer-Skarke database
****************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        kreuzerSkarkeDim3()
  * Outputs:
      * a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, A list of *note KSEntry: KSEntry,'s,
        each one representing one of the 4319 polytopes (including description
        header information). Use *note matrix(KSEntry): matrix_lpKSEntry_rp, to
        make any element in this list into something usable from Macaulay2.

Description
===========

As a an example, let's take the 101th example on this list.

+-------------------------------------------+
|i1 : topes = kreuzerSkarkeDim3();          |
+-------------------------------------------+
|i2 : #topes                                |
|                                           |
|o2 = 4319                                  |
+-------------------------------------------+
|i3 : tope = topes_100                      |
|                                           |
|o3 = 3 5  M:12 5 N:15 5 Pic:13 Cor:4 id:100|
|         1    0    0   -3    1             |
|         0    1    0    0   -2             |
|         0    0    1   -2    2             |
|                                           |
|o3 : KSEntry                               |
+-------------------------------------------+
|i4 : header = description tope             |
|                                           |
|o4 = 3 5  M:12 5 N:15 5 Pic:13 Cor:4 id:100|
+-------------------------------------------+
|i5 : A = matrix tope                       |
|                                           |
|o5 = | 1 0 0 -3 1  |                       |
|     | 0 1 0 0  -2 |                       |
|     | 0 0 1 -2 2  |                       |
|                                           |
|              3       5                    |
|o5 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ                     |
+-------------------------------------------+

The first line gives some information about the example, see *note
Kreuzer-Skarke description headers: Kreuzer-Skarke description headers, for
more details. The polytope is the convex hull of the columns of the matrix $A$.

One can use the packages *note Polyhedra: (Polyhedra)Top, and *note
NormalToricVarieties: (NormalToricVarieties)Top, to investigate these
