KSEntry -- an entry from the Kreuzer-Skarke database of dimension 3 and 4 reflexive polytopes
*********************************************************************************************

Description
===========

A KSEntry is essentially a string containing a description header and the
vertices of a reflexive polytope.  We have given it its own type for ease of
use in Macaulay2.



The most common way to obtain (lists of) KSEntry's is via a call *note
kreuzerSkarke: kreuzerSkarke, or *note kreuzerSkarkeDim3: kreuzerSkarkeDim3,.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : L = kreuzerSkarke(3, Limit=>5)                                          |
|using offline data file: ks3-n244.txt                                        |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = {4 5  M:53 5 N:9 5 H:3,43 [-80] id:0, 4 5  M:48 5 N:8 5 H:3,45 [-84]    |
|         1   0   2   4 -10                    1   0   2   4  -8              |
|         0   1   3   5  -9                    0   1   5   3  -9              |
|         0   0   4   0  -4                    0   0   6   0  -6              |
|         0   0   0   8  -8                    0   0   0   6  -6              |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     id:1, 4 6  M:48 6 N:8 6 H:3,45 [-84] id:2, 4 13  M:64 13 N:8            |
|              1   1   0   2   4  -8                1   0   0   2             |
|              0   3   0   2   0  -6                0   1   1   3             |
|              0   0   1  -1   3  -3                0   0   4   0             |
|              0   0   0   0   6  -6                0   0   0   4             |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     7 H:3,51 [-96] id:3               , 4 9  M:66 9 N:8 6 H:3,57            |
|     -2   0  -1  -1   0   2   2  -3  -3     1   0   0   1  -3   3            |
|     -5   2   0   0   2   4   4  -6  -6     0   1   0   0   2  -4            |
|     -4   5   4  -1   0   1   0  -4  -5     0   0   1   0   2  -2            |
|     -4   1  -1  -1   1   5   5  -5  -5     0   0   0   2   0  -4            |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     [-108] id:4}                                                            |
|       3  -3   5                                                             |
|      -6   4  -8                                                             |
|      -2   0  -4                                                             |
|      -6   6  -6                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : netList L                                                               |
|                                                                             |
|     +----------------------------------------------------+                  |
|o2 = |4 5  M:53 5 N:9 5 H:3,43 [-80] id:0                 |                  |
|     |   1   0   2   4 -10                                |                  |
|     |   0   1   3   5  -9                                |                  |
|     |   0   0   4   0  -4                                |                  |
|     |   0   0   0   8  -8                                |                  |
|     +----------------------------------------------------+                  |
|     |4 5  M:48 5 N:8 5 H:3,45 [-84] id:1                 |                  |
|     |   1   0   2   4  -8                                |                  |
|     |   0   1   5   3  -9                                |                  |
|     |   0   0   6   0  -6                                |                  |
|     |   0   0   0   6  -6                                |                  |
|     +----------------------------------------------------+                  |
|     |4 6  M:48 6 N:8 6 H:3,45 [-84] id:2                 |                  |
|     |   1   1   0   2   4  -8                            |                  |
|     |   0   3   0   2   0  -6                            |                  |
|     |   0   0   1  -1   3  -3                            |                  |
|     |   0   0   0   0   6  -6                            |                  |
|     +----------------------------------------------------+                  |
|     |4 13  M:64 13 N:8 7 H:3,51 [-96] id:3               |                  |
|     |   1   0   0   2  -2   0  -1  -1   0   2   2  -3  -3|                  |
|     |   0   1   1   3  -5   2   0   0   2   4   4  -6  -6|                  |
|     |   0   0   4   0  -4   5   4  -1   0   1   0  -4  -5|                  |
|     |   0   0   0   4  -4   1  -1  -1   1   5   5  -5  -5|                  |
|     +----------------------------------------------------+                  |
|     |4 9  M:66 9 N:8 6 H:3,57 [-108] id:4                |                  |
|     |   1   0   0   1  -3   3   3  -3   5                |                  |
|     |   0   1   0   0   2  -4  -6   4  -8                |                  |
|     |   0   0   1   0   2  -2  -2   0  -4                |                  |
|     |   0   0   0   2   0  -4  -6   6  -6                |                  |
|     +----------------------------------------------------+                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Once one has a KSEntry, the most important function is to extract the matrix
whose columns are the vertices of the corresponding polytope.

+-----------------------+
|i3 : A = matrix L_0    |
|                       |
|o3 = | 1 0 2 4 -10 |   |
|     | 0 1 3 5 -9  |   |
|     | 0 0 4 0 -4  |   |
|     | 0 0 0 8 -8  |   |
|                       |
|              4       5|
|o3 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ |
+-----------------------+

Although the most common way to create (lists of) KSEntry's is via a call to
*note kreuzerSkarke: kreuzerSkarke, or *note kreuzerSkarkeDim3:
kreuzerSkarkeDim3, as above, it is also possible to start with a string that
perhaps you found while searching the Kreuzer-Skarke database directly.

+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : e = KSEntry "4 5  M:53 5 N:9 5 H:3,43 [-80] id:0|
|       1   0   2   4 -10                             |
|       0   1   3   5  -9                             |
|       0   0   4   0  -4                             |
|       0   0   0   8  -8                             |
|       ";                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : A = matrix e                                    |
|                                                     |
|o5 = | 1 0 2 4 -10 |                                 |
|     | 0 1 3 5 -9  |                                 |
|     | 0 0 4 0 -4  |                                 |
|     | 0 0 0 8 -8  |                                 |
|                                                     |
|              4       5                              |
|o5 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ                               |
+-----------------------------------------------------+

