toExternalString(KSEntry) -- a string suitable for input to Macaulay2
*********************************************************************

  * Function: *note toExternalString: (Macaulay2Doc)toExternalString,
  * Usage: 
        toExternalString e
  * Inputs:
      * e, an *note entry from the Kreuzer-Skarke database: KSEntry,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String,, 

Description
===========

Returns the underlying string of the given entry from the Kreuzer-Skarke
database.

+---------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : e = KSEntry "4 5  M:53 5 N:9 5 H:3,43 [-80] id:0                      |
|       1   0   2   4 -10                                                   |
|       0   1   3   5  -9                                                   |
|       0   0   4   0  -4                                                   |
|       0   0   0   8  -8                                                   |
|       ";                                                                  |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : str = toExternalString e                                              |
|                                                                           |
|o2 = KSEntry "4 5  M:53 5 N:9 5 H:3,43 [-80] id:0\n  1   0   2   4 -10\n  0|
|     1   3   5  -9\n  0   0   4   0  -4\n  0   0   0   8  -8\n  "          |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------------+

The main value of this function, is that one can use this string as input to
Macaulay2.

+----------------------------------------+
|i3 : e1 = value str                     |
|                                        |
|o3 = 4 5  M:53 5 N:9 5 H:3,43 [-80] id:0|
|       1   0   2   4 -10                |
|       0   1   3   5  -9                |
|       0   0   4   0  -4                |
|       0   0   0   8  -8                |
|                                        |
|                                        |
|o3 : KSEntry                            |
+----------------------------------------+
|i4 : e1 === e                           |
|                                        |
|o4 = true                               |
+----------------------------------------+

